.\" Vajra — Break noise. Preserve truth.
.TH VAJRA 1 "2026-04-08" "vajra 0.1.0" "Vajra Manual"
.SH NAME
vajra \- deterministic semantic reduction engine for structured data
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B vajra
[\fIGLOBAL OPTIONS\fR]
.I COMMAND
[\fICOMMAND OPTIONS\fR]
[\fIARGS\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B Vajra
analyzes arbitrary structured data \(em JSON, YAML, CSV, NDJSON, Markdown, and PDF
\(em extracts structural fingerprints, computes entropy and statistical profiles,
detects anomalies and schema drift, discovers cross-field relationships, and
renders deterministic essences optimized for humans, auditors, and AI pipelines.
.PP
Every analysis is deterministic: the same input with the same configuration
always produces byte-identical output.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B inspect \fIINPUT\fR
Full structural analysis. Shows document metadata, all wildcard paths with
types and counts, BLAKE3 fingerprints, and domain type recognition.
.TP
.B stats \fIINPUT\fR
Statistical summary. Per-path Shannon entropy, cardinality, frequency
distributions, numeric statistics (min, max, median, MAD, percentiles),
and top values.
.TP
.B anomalies \fIINPUT\fR
Anomaly detection. MAD-based numeric outliers, rarity scoring via
self-information, and type instability detection.
.TP
.B fingerprint \fIINPUT\fR
Structural fingerprints. BLAKE3 path-set hash, typed-path hash, Merkle
shape hash, and repeated motif frequencies.
.TP
.B essence \fIINPUT\fR
Generate a concern-oriented essence. Scores observations using the active
profile's weight vector, ranks by importance, and renders in the requested
format. Supports token budgets for LLM context window optimization.
.TP
.B drift \fIBASELINE\fR \fICANDIDATE\fR
Schema drift detection between two documents. Reports added/removed paths,
type changes, and distributional shifts measured by Jensen-Shannon Divergence
and 1D Wasserstein distance. Classifies severity as None/Low/Medium/High/Critical.
.TP
.B cluster \fIINPUTS...\fR
Cluster similar documents by structural similarity. Uses MinHash signatures
with Locality-Sensitive Hashing for scalable nearest-neighbor search.
Accepts files or directories.
.TP
.B invariants \fIINPUT\fR [\fB\-\-top\-k\fR \fIN\fR]
Discover cross-field relationships via conditional entropy and pointwise
mutual information. Reports functional dependencies and co-occurrence patterns.
.TP
.B query \fIINPUT\fR \fIEXPRESSION\fR
Run a query expression against a document. Supports path expressions
($.a[*].b), analysis functions (entropy, cardinality, null_rate, instability,
count, rarity, depth), and comparisons (entropy($.x) > 0.5).
.TP
.B batch \fIDIRECTORY\fR
Parallel batch analysis of all JSON files in a directory using Rayon.
Reports per-document summaries and aggregate statistics including common
and rare paths.
.TP
.B profiles
List all available profiles (built-in and custom from \fB\-\-config\fR).
.SH GLOBAL OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-format " FORMAT"
Output format. One of: \fBtext\fR (default), \fBjson\fR, \fBmarkdown\fR,
\fBcompact-ai\fR. The compact-ai format uses short keys and aggressive
compression for LLM token efficiency.
.TP
.BI \-\-profile " NAME"
Concern profile for scoring and rendering. Built-in profiles: \fBstaff\fR
(plain language, narrative), \fBengineer\fR (technical, balanced),
\fBauditor\fR (formal, completeness-focused), \fBai\fR (compact, machine-parseable),
\fBfraud\fR (investigative, outlier-focused). Default: \fBengineer\fR.
.TP
.BI \-\-config " PATH"
Path to a TOML configuration file containing custom profile definitions.
.TP
.BI \-\-budget " N"
Token budget for essence output. Observations are selected by score-per-token
ratio using a greedy knapsack algorithm until the budget is exhausted.
.TP
.BI \-\-input\-format " FORMAT"
Force input format instead of auto-detecting. One of: \fBjson\fR, \fBndjson\fR,
\fByaml\fR, \fBcsv\fR, \fBtsv\fR, \fBmarkdown\fR, \fBpdf\fR.
.TP
.B \-\-redact
Apply built-in redaction patterns (SSN, email, phone, credit card) before output.
Uses deterministic BLAKE3 hashing so redacted values can still be correlated.
.TP
.B \-\-streaming
Force streaming analysis pipeline. Uses DDSketch for quantiles, Count-Min
Sketch for frequency estimation, and Space-Saving for top-k detection.
Bounded memory regardless of document size.
.TP
.B \-\-quiet
Suppress progress output.
.TP
.B \-\-explain
Include score decomposition in essence output.
.SH INPUT FORMATS
.B Vajra
auto-detects input format from file extension and content:
.PP
.RS
.nf
.B Extension        Format
\&.json             JSON
\&.ndjson, .jsonl   Newline-delimited JSON
\&.yaml, .yml       YAML (multi-document supported)
\&.csv              Comma-separated values
\&.tsv              Tab-separated values
\&.md, .markdown    Markdown
\&.pdf              PDF (text extraction)
\&.gz               Gzip compressed (any format)
\&.zst, .zstd       Zstd compressed (any format)
http://, https://  HTTP URL (fetched automatically)
\-                  Standard input
.fi
.RE
.PP
Double extensions are supported: \fB.json.gz\fR decompresses then parses as JSON.
.SH PROFILES
.SS staff
Weights: anomaly_strength=0.30, structural_coverage=0.25, concern_relevance=0.20.
Plain vocabulary, narrative sections: "What Stands Out", "What This Likely Means".
.SS engineer
Weights: instability=0.25, balanced across all dimensions.
Technical vocabulary with JSONPath paths and metric values.
.SS auditor
Weights: concern_relevance=0.30, instability=0.20, anomaly_strength=0.20.
Formal language with numbered findings and completeness assessment.
.SS ai
Weights: entropy_signal=0.20, structural_coverage=0.20, anomaly_strength=0.20.
Terse machine-parseable output. In compact-ai format, uses short keys
(p=path, t=type, s=score) and includes a "drill" section for follow-up queries.
.SS fraud
Weights: anomaly_strength=0.35, rarity=0.25.
Investigative framing with RISK/ALERT labels for outliers and suspicious patterns.
.SH ALGORITHMS
All algorithms satisfy three gates: O(n) or O(n log n) time complexity,
published and peer-reviewed, and fully deterministic.
.PP
.B BLAKE3
\(em All hashing (O'Connor et al. 2020). 3-7x faster than SHA-256.
.PP
.B Shannon Entropy
\(em Value diversity measurement. Distinguishes boilerplate from signal.
.PP
.B MAD
\(em Median Absolute Deviation for robust outlier detection. 50% breakdown point.
.PP
.B DDSketch
\(em Streaming quantile estimation with relative error guarantees (Masson et al. 2019).
.PP
.B Count-Min Sketch
\(em Streaming frequency estimation with conservative update (Cormode & Muthukrishnan 2005).
.PP
.B Jensen-Shannon Divergence
\(em Distribution comparison. Symmetric, bounded [0,1], proper metric via sqrt
(Endres & Schindelin 2003).
.PP
.B MinHash + LSH
\(em Scalable similarity search. O(n) indexing, sublinear queries
(Broder 1997, Indyk & Motwani 1998).
.SH EXAMPLES
Inspect a JSON file:
.PP
.RS
.nf
vajra inspect data.json
.fi
.RE
.PP
Generate an essence for non-technical staff:
.PP
.RS
.nf
vajra essence claims.json --profile staff --format markdown
.fi
.RE
.PP
Detect drift between API versions:
.PP
.RS
.nf
vajra drift v1.json v2.json
.fi
.RE
.PP
Compact AI-ready output with token budget:
.PP
.RS
.nf
vajra essence data.json --profile ai --format compact-ai --budget 500
.fi
.RE
.PP
Query entropy of a specific field:
.PP
.RS
.nf
vajra query data.json 'entropy($.claims[*].status)'
.fi
.RE
.PP
Analyze a gzipped NDJSON batch from a URL:
.PP
.RS
.nf
vajra stats https://api.example.com/events.ndjson.gz
.fi
.RE
.PP
Pipe from stdin with redaction:
.PP
.RS
.nf
curl -s https://api.example.com/patient | vajra essence - --profile staff --redact
.fi
.RE
.SH FILES
.TP
.B ~/.vajra/config.toml
Default configuration file location (optional).
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
Analysis completed but anomalies found (with \fB\-\-strict\fR).
.TP
.B 2
Input error (file not found, parse failure).
.TP
.B 3
Configuration error (invalid profile, bad config file).
